            <ArticleTitle>The chronic pain initiative and community care of North Carolina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>237-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The rate of unintentional deaths from opioid poisoning has reached epidemic proportions. One model of successful intervention is Project Lazarus, an integrated-care pilot program in Wilkes County, North Carolina. Community Care of North Carolina, supported by a grant of $1.3 million from the Kate B. Reynolds Charitable Trust and matching funds of $1.3 million from the North Carolina Office of Rural Health and Community Care, is now expanding the Project Lazarus approach statewide.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
